# Public repository hygiene

This repository is **public**. Treat every commit as world-readable.

## Never commit

- Real secrets: `abk_live_*` / long `abk_test_*`, `whsec_*` (except obvious placeholders like `whsec_test`), private keys, npm/NuGet/PyPI tokens, GPG key material, `.env` files
- Operator-only Cursor rules that name private apps, Railway wiring, or internal promote paths (keep those in **private** repos only)
- Local build junk: `**/.build/`, `.venv/`, `vendor/`, `nupkg/` with credentials
- Machine home paths or personal employer emails in new file contents

## Do not publish in docs / README / DEPLOY

- Links to **private** GitHub repos (e.g. hosting or platform) — say “private Autlantic app repos” or link [docs.autlantic.com](https://docs.autlantic.com) instead
- Stale monorepo commands that no longer exist here (`pnpm dev:billing-api`, `apps/billing-api`, etc.)
- Internal hostnames, database URLs, or Railway project IDs

## Allowed placeholders

- `abk_test_local`, `abk_test_x`, `whsec_test`, `whsec_demo_*`, demo EVM addresses used in examples

## Before finishing a change on a public repo

1. Grep the diff for secrets and private GitHub URLs.
2. Prefer hosted public API (`https://billing.autlantic.com`) over private runbooks.
3. If guidance is only for Autlantic operators, put it in a **private** repo — not here.

See also root `DEPLOY.md` and `SECURITY.md` when present.
